message.content:
To get the CNAME records for **sample.com** you’ll hit the domain endpoint and then pull the IDs that VirusTotal returns for the CNAME objects.

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com
Authorization: Bearer secret123
```

The JSON response will look roughly like this:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "id": "sample.com",
    "type": "domains",
    "attributes": { … },
    "relationships": {
      "cname_records": {
        "data": [
          { "id": "cname1", "type": "cname_records" },
          { "id": "cname2", "type": "cname_records" },
          …
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Only the IDs you need are:**

- Domain ID: `sample.com`
- CNAME record IDs: `cname1`, `cname2`, … (the values inside `relationships.cname_records.data[*].id`)

So, after making the request, extract those `id` fields – that’s all you need.
